  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-0ce050ba-7fff-bad3-5d17-47e497923db6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed advertisement, by reason of its inappropriate scale and location, would result in an overbearing, incongruous and overly prominent form of advertisement, to the detriment of the significance of the host Locally Listed building and it&#x27;s setting, the setting of adjacent Grade II* Hackney Empire and Grade II Hackney Town Hall and would fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Hackney Town Hall Conservation Area. The proposal is therefore deemed contrary to Hackney Local Development Plan (LP33)(2020) policies PP1 (Public Realm), LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets), LP4 (Non-Designated Heritage Assets), LP7 (Advertisements), London Plan (2021) policies D3 (Optimising Site Capacity through the Design-Led Approach), D8 (Public Realm), HC1 (Heritage Conservation and Growth) and the Hackney Town Hall Conservation Area Appraisal (2000).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
